content.text:
I've published the wording report as a new private artifact: https://claude.ai/artifact/UKKhGdhBUbrcjPooPtcsDL. It lists about 35 places on JusPrin's own screens where a first-time user would misread the text or get stuck. I changed no code and put nothing on the JusPrin v2 canvas. The artifact is private, so Kenneth can only open the link once it's shared with him from the page's Share menu.

The report is grouped by screen: Home, print history, project chat, printer chat, Preferences, the OrcaSlicer import, the welcome-back window and the main window. Each problem has:
- the screenshot and the exact current text;
- what a person would think it means;
- a proposed rewording, marked as a proposal;
- the code location showing the proposal is true;
- whether a fresh reader who only saw the screenshots caught it, or only my own reading did.

Some of the bigger problems:
- **Settings items that open a chat:** "Printer settings…" on Home and "Filament settings…" in the filament menu both open a chat panel, not a settings window.
- **Claims the app can't know:** history says "never printed" for G-code that was exported and may have been printed from a card. A project with exported G-code is still labelled "Draft".
- **"Send report" doesn't send:** the button in the printer chat only saves the report on this computer.
- **Earlier-chat restore:** the dialog shows a raw machine timestamp ("2026-10-03T12:00:00Z"). Its notices never say that restoring replaces the current work, and two failure messages ("corrupt", "needs recovery") offer no way out.
- **Report form:** "0 of 200 characters" is a minimum, but every reader took it as a maximum.
- **Welcome back:** people coming from JusPrin v1 are offered sign-up with no word that their v1 account doesn't carry over.

On first launch, which another session is fixing, I found no regressions. I found four problems the 6 November review didn't list. The worst is that the page still says "Sign up to use the AI agent, or skip it" and offers "Just slice for now" after the person has signed in.

The native screens are close-ups drawn by the shell test harness from its test project, not full windows. Whole-window captures came out black because the screen was locked.

Three proposals depend on things I couldn't confirm, and the report marks each "unverified":
- whether starting a new chat clears the "Project restoration needs recovery" block;
- whether the browser sign-in page also lets a new person sign up;
- whether the server sends the per-message credit prices to the app.

The report ends with six "Decision needed" paragraphs for Kenneth:
- whether the two settings menu items keep opening a chat under a new name, or open the settings window;
- whether to take the G-code hash codes off the screen;
- how to word prints JusPrin didn't see finish, including removing "last print failed", which goes against the 27 October rule;
- whether to hide, rename or build out "Send report";
- one name for the agent everywhere;
- whether the welcome-back window promises to move v1 subscriptions.

A hand-over note with the working-file paths is in the shared notes folder, as `wording-sweep-2026-11-06.md`.

